BT /F2 13 Tf 54 398.4 Td (When to Use What?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 363.2 Td (Use SQL When...  |  Use NoSQL When...) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 350.6 Td (Data has clear structure  |  Data changes shape often) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 338.0 Td (You need complex queries  |  You need super fast reads) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 325.4 Td (Banking, e-commerce  |  Social media, gaming) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 312.8 Td (Relationships matter  |  Scale is massive) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 276.2 Td (Memory Trick) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 255.0 Td (* SQL = Structured Query Language = Everything in neat boxes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 241.0 Td (* NoSQL = Not Only SQL = Flexible, like a backpack \(throw anything in\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 203.0 Td (ACID Properties \(SQL's Superpowers\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 181.8 Td (* Atomicity: All or nothing \(like a bank transfer - both accounts change or neither\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 167.8 Td (* Consistency: Rules are always followed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 153.8 Td (* Isolation: Transactions don't mess with each other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 139.8 Td (* Durability: Once saved, it stays saved forever) Tj ET
endstream
