BT /F2 16 Tf 54 584.8 Td (DAY 6: Scaling - Handling More Users) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 533.4 Td (The Big Idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 512.2 Td (Imagine your lemonade stand gets super popular. Yesterday 10 people came. Today) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 498.2 Td (10,000 people want lemonade! What do you do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 470.2 Td (Scaling = Making your system handle more users without breaking.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 432.2 Td (Two Ways to Scale) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 397.0 Td (1. Vertical Scaling \(Scale UP\) - Get a BIGGER Machine) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 383.0 Td (* Like replacing your bicycle with a motorcycle) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 369.0 Td (* Buy a more powerful server \(more RAM, CPU, storage\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 355.0 Td (* Simple but has limits \(you can't make one machine infinitely powerful\)) Tj ET
