BT /F2 13 Tf 54 720.0 Td (Replication Lag) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 698.8 Td (* The time it takes for slave to get master's latest data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 684.8 Td (* Usually milliseconds, but can be seconds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 670.8 Td (* Problem: User writes to master, reads from slave, doesn't see their own update!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 632.8 Td (Solution: Read-Your-Own-Writes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 611.6 Td (* After a user writes, read from MASTER for that user) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597.6 Td (* Everyone else reads from slaves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 583.6 Td (* Best of both worlds!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 545.6 Td (Today's Quiz) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524.4 Td (1. Why can't all databases be masters?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 510.4 Td (2. What is replication lag?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 496.4 Td (3. If the master dies, what happens?) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 54 424.4 Td (DAY 12: Database Sharding - Splitting Data) Tj ET
