BT /F2 13 Tf 54 720.0 Td (The Big Idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 698.8 Td (Consistent hashing is like arranging people in a circle instead of a line. When) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 684.8 Td (someone leaves or joins, only their neighbors are affected, not everyone!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 646.8 Td (The Problem It Solves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625.6 Td (Regular hashing: server = hash\(key\) % N) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 611.6 Td (* If you add/remove a server \(N changes\), EVERYTHING moves!) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597.6 Td (* Like rearranging ALL lockers when one new locker is added.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 569.6 Td (Consistent hashing:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555.6 Td (* Only ~1/N of the data moves when a server changes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541.6 Td (* Like adding a new seat at a round table - only neighbors shift) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 503.6 Td (How It Works) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 478.4 Td (  Imagine a clock \(circle from 0 to 360 degrees\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 465.8 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 453.2 Td (          0/360) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 440.6 Td (           |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 428.0 Td (     Server A \(at 90\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 415.4 Td (           |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 402.8 Td (     330 --+-- 90) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 390.2 Td (           |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 377.6 Td (     Server C \(at 210\)    Server B \(at 150\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 365.0 Td (           |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 352.4 Td (          180) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 339.8 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 327.2 Td (  Data "photo_123" hashes to position 120 -> goes to Server B \(next clockwise\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 314.6 Td (  Data "video_456" hashes to position 200 -> goes to Server C \(next clockwise\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 274.0 Td (When a Server Joins/Leaves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 252.8 Td (* Server B dies: Only B's data moves to next server \(C\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 238.8 Td (* Other servers are NOT affected!) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 224.8 Td (* Compare: Regular hashing would reshuffle everything) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 186.8 Td (Memory Trick) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 165.6 Td (Think of it as a CLOCK - data goes to the next server clockwise. Adding/removing a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 151.6 Td (server only affects the slice next to it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 113.6 Td (Virtual Nodes \(Making it Even\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 92.4 Td (Problem: Servers might be unevenly spaced on the circle) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 78.4 Td (Solution: Each real server gets multiple positions \(virtual nodes\)) Tj ET
endstream
