BT /F2 13 Tf 54 380.4 Td (The Big Idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 359.2 Td (The CAP Theorem says that in a distributed system, you can only have 2 out of 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 345.2 Td (things. It's like saying you can only pick 2 toppings on your pizza, never all 3!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 307.2 Td (The Three Properties) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272.0 Td (C - Consistency: Every read gets the LATEST data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 258.0 Td (* Like: Everyone sees the same scoreboard at the same time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 230.0 Td (A - Availability: System ALWAYS responds \(never says "come back later"\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 216.0 Td (* Like: The store is ALWAYS open, never closed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 188.0 Td (P - Partition Tolerance: System works even if network breaks between servers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 174.0 Td (* Like: The school still functions even if the intercom breaks) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 136.0 Td (The Rule) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 114.8 Td (In real distributed systems, network issues WILL happen \(P is required\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 100.8 Td (So you really choose between:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 86.8 Td (* CP \(Consistency + Partition Tolerance\): Always correct data, might be unavailable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 72.8 Td (sometimes) Tj ET
endstream
