BT /F2 16 Tf 54 634.0 Td (DAY 23: Hashing & Checksums) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 582.6 Td (The Big Idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 561.4 Td (Hashing is like a fingerprint for data. You take any data \(a file, password, message\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 547.4 Td (and create a fixed-size unique identifier.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 509.4 Td (Properties of a Good Hash) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 488.2 Td (1. Same input = Same output \(always\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 474.2 Td (2. Different input = Different output \(usually\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 460.2 Td (3. Can't reverse it \(can't get original from hash\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 446.2 Td (4. Small change = Completely different hash) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 408.2 Td (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 383.0 Td (  hash\("Hello"\) = "2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c...") Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 370.4 Td (  hash\("hello"\) = "b6ef26b11e18305c6c4aa87e5bfe7e0a2818c5f3...") Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 357.8 Td (  hash\("Hello!"\) = "9b71d224bd62f3785d96d46ad3ea3d73319bfbc2...") Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 341.2 Td (Notice: Tiny changes create completely different hashes!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 303.2 Td (Use Cases) Tj ET
