BT /F2 13 Tf 54 432.2 Td (The Big Idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 411.0 Td (Idempotent means doing something multiple times has the SAME effect as doing it once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 397.0 Td (Like pressing an elevator button - pressing it 5 times doesn't make the elevator come) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 383.0 Td (5 times faster!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 345.0 Td (Why Idempotency Matters) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 319.8 Td (  Scenario: You click "Pay $100" button) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 307.2 Td (  Network glitch: Your phone doesn't get the response) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 294.6 Td (  Phone retries: Sends payment request again) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 282.0 Td (  WITHOUT idempotency: You get charged $200!) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 269.4 Td (  WITH idempotency: You get charged $100 \(second request is ignored\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 228.8 Td (Idempotent vs Non-Idempotent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 207.6 Td (Operation  |  Idempotent?  |  Why) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 195.0 Td (GET /users/123  |  Yes  |  Reading doesn't change anything) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 182.4 Td (DELETE /users/123  |  Yes  |  Deleting twice = same as once) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 169.8 Td (PUT /users/123 {name: "Bob"}  |  Yes  |  Setting to same value repeatedly) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 157.2 Td (POST /orders  |  NO!  |  Creates new order each time) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 144.6 Td (POST /payments  |  Must make it so!  |  Use idempotency key) Tj ET
