BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371.0 Td (In distributed systems, failure is not IF but WHEN. Great system designers don't try) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 357.0 Td (to prevent ALL failures - they design systems that SURVIVE failures gracefully!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 319.0 Td (Types of Failures) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 297.8 Td (1. Hardware: Disk dies, server crashes, network card fails) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 283.8 Td (2. Software: Bug causes crash, memory leak, deadlock) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 269.8 Td (3. Network: Packet loss, partition, latency spike) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 255.8 Td (4. Human: Wrong config deployed, wrong server shut down) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 241.8 Td (5. Dependencies: Third-party API down, cloud region outage) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 203.8 Td (Failure Design Patterns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 168.6 Td (1. Graceful Degradation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 154.6 Td (* When part of system fails, reduce features but stay alive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 140.6 Td (* Netflix: If recommendation service dies, show popular titles instead) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 126.6 Td (* Amazon: If review service dies, show product without reviews) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 98.6 Td (2. Bulkhead Pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 84.6 Td (* Isolate components so one failure doesn't sink everything) Tj ET
endstream
