BT /F1 9 Tf 64 427.4 Td (  - Each chunk stored on 3 different servers \(replication factor = 3\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 414.8 Td (  - Master knows: Chunk 1 is on Server A, B, D) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 402.2 Td (                  Chunk 2 is on Server B, C, E) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 389.6 Td (                  ...) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 349.0 Td (Read Flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 323.8 Td (  1. Client asks Master: "Where is video.mp4?") Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 311.2 Td (  2. Master replies: "Chunks 1-5, here are their locations") Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 298.6 Td (  3. Client reads directly from Chunk Servers \(no bottleneck on Master!\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 286.0 Td (  4. Client can read different chunks from different servers in parallel) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 245.4 Td (Write Flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 220.2 Td (  1. Client asks Master: "I want to write new_file.txt") Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 207.6 Td (  2. Master allocates chunks, picks 3 servers per chunk) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 195.0 Td (  3. Client sends data to first server) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 182.4 Td (  4. First server replicates to second, second to third \(pipeline\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 169.8 Td (  5. All confirm -> Write successful!) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 129.2 Td (Handling Failures) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 108.0 Td (* Chunk Server dies: Master detects via heartbeat, re-replicates chunks from other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 94.0 Td (copies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 80.0 Td (* Master dies: Standby master takes over \(has replicated metadata\)) Tj ET
