stream
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 720.0 Td (  If ANY said "No" in Phase 1:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 707.4 Td (  Coordinator: "ABORT!" --> All services rollback) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 666.8 Td (Problems with 2PC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 645.6 Td (* Blocking: If coordinator dies between phases, participants wait forever) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631.6 Td (* Single Point of Failure: Coordinator is critical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 617.6 Td (* Performance: Holding locks during entire protocol is slow) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 579.6 Td (Three-Phase Commit \(3PC\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558.4 Td (Adds a "pre-commit" phase to reduce blocking:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 540.4 Td (  Phase 1: Can Commit? \(VOTE\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 527.8 Td (  Phase 2: Pre-Commit \(PREPARE - but don't commit yet\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 515.2 Td (  Phase 3: Do Commit \(ACTUALLY commit\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 498.6 Td (* If coordinator dies after Phase 2, participants can decide themselves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 484.6 Td (* Less blocking, but more messages) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 446.6 Td (Modern Alternative: Saga Pattern \(Revisited\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 421.4 Td (  Instead of distributed transaction:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 408.8 Td (  Execute steps in sequence, compensate on failure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 396.2 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 383.6 Td (  Step 1: Debit Account A \($100\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 371.0 Td (  Step 2: Credit Account B \($100\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 358.4 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 345.8 Td (  If Step 2 fails:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 64 333.2 Td (  Compensate Step 1: Credit Account A \($100\) \(undo the debit\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 292.6 Td (Comparison) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 271.4 Td (Approach  |  Consistency  |  Performance  |  Complexity) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 258.8 Td (2PC  |  Strong  |  Slow \(blocking\)  |  Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 246.2 Td (3PC  |  Strong  |  Better  |  High) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 233.6 Td (Saga  |  Eventual  |  Fast  |  Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 221.0 Td (Event Sourcing  |  Eventual  |  Fast  |  High) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 184.4 Td (When to Use What) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 163.2 Td (* 2PC: When you MUST have strong consistency \(banking between systems\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 149.2 Td (* Saga: When eventual consistency is acceptable \(e-commerce orders\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 135.2 Td (* Event Sourcing: When you need audit trail + eventual consistency) Tj ET
endstream
